# The trainer image is built from the repository root so it can carry the Python SDK
# alongside the workload. Without this, the build context would include node_modules and
# the git history — hundreds of megabytes shipped to the daemon to produce a 60 MB image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github
coverage
*.log

# The dataset reaches the ResNet image as a named build context (`--build-context
# cifar=...`), which is the whole point of that flag: it is 341 MB, and without this line
# it would be sent to the daemon again on every build of every other image.
data

# Nothing in the control plane belongs in a training or serving image.
packages
db
api
docs
deploy/local

# Except the router, which *is* a control-plane component and is built from here. It needs
# its own package and one file from the server: `domain/routing.js`, which is pure and
# imports nothing, so it travels alone. Copying it rather than reimplementing it is the
# point — the control plane stores the weights and the router applies them, and two
# implementations of what a weight means would be two answers to the question §21 exists
# to make answerable.
!packages/router
!packages/server/src/domain/routing.js
